  "id": "Compound::DB01181 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Ifosfamide is shown to bind to Cyp2c18 and Cyp2c8, which are both involved in the metabolism of endogenous substrates. These enzymes are part of the Cyp2b6 pathway, which is associated with steroid hydroxylase activity and arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity. The evidence suggests that Ifosfamide may influence Cyp2b6 through its interaction with these related cytochrome P450 enzymes, potentially modulating their activity. The final scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Ifosfamide to Cyp2b6 suggests a broader role in metabolic processes, but the specific mechanism by which Ifosfamide affects Cyp2b6 requires further investigation.",
